@startuml libcpg-integration-boundaries
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

title <b>libcpg integration boundaries</b>\n<size:11><i>dependency arrows point from consumers to providers; evidence crosses a separate boundary</i></size>

package "Semantic leaves" #E8F5E9 {
  component "llattice v2\njoin/meet/lattice laws" as Lattice #C8E6C9
  component "libvgraph\nCSR · iterative SCC · quotient DAG" as Graph #A5D6A7
  component "libmorphism\nsemantic descriptors and law evidence" as Morphism #81C784
}

component "libcpg\nanalysis producer and selective consumer" as Libcpg #BBDEFB
component "vinary-libcpg-adapter\nfreshness · digest · trust · independence" as Adapter #FFE0B2
component "Vinary assurance boundary\ncandidate report + independent guarantee" as Assurance #F8BBD0
component "lling-llang\nindependent optimization library" as LlingLlang #FFF9C4
component "optional libcpg integration\none-way use of public lling-llang APIs" as OptionalIntegration #D1C4E9

Libcpg ..> Lattice : depends on lawful dataflow vocabulary
Libcpg ..> Graph : depends on structural graph substrate
Adapter ..> Morphism : depends on evidence vocabulary
Adapter ..> Libcpg : consumes immutable candidate reports
Adapter --> Assurance : bound assurance artifact
OptionalIntegration ..> Libcpg : consumes public analysis API
OptionalIntegration ..> LlingLlang : consumes public optimizer API

note bottom of Libcpg
  libcpg core remains independently
  usable and owns analysis semantics.
end note

note bottom of OptionalIntegration
  This boundary may live behind an
  optional libcpg feature or adapter.
  lling-llang is not part of libcpg,
  and lling-llang never depends on libcpg.
end note

legend right
  |<#C8E6C9> algebraic semantic leaf |
  |<#A5D6A7> structural graph leaf |
  |<#81C784> evidence semantic leaf |
  |<#BBDEFB> analysis producer |
  |<#FFE0B2> validation adapter |
  |<#F8BBD0> assurance boundary |
  |<#FFF9C4> independent optimizer |
  |<#D1C4E9> optional one-way integration |
endlegend
@enduml
